321	Instructions for Recipient
322	The information provided may be different for covered and noncovered
323	securities. For a description of covered securities, see the Instructions for
324	Form 8949. For a taxable covered security acquired at a premium, unless you
325	notified the payer in writing in accordance with Regulations section
326	1.6045-1(n)(5) that you did not want to amortize the premium under section 171,
327	or for a tax-exempt covered security acquired at a premium, your payer must
328	generally report either (1) a net amount of interest that reflects the offset of the
329	amount of interest paid to you by the amount of premium amortization allocable
330	to the payment(s), or (2) a gross amount for both the interest paid to you and the
331	premium amortization allocable to the payment(s). If you did notify your payer
332	that you did not want to amortize the premium on a taxable covered security,
333	then your payer will only report the gross amount of interest paid to you. For a
334	noncovered security acquired at a premium, your payer is only required to report
335	the gross amount of interest paid to you.
336	Recipient’s taxpayer identification number (TIN). For your protection, this
337	form may show only the last four digits of your TIN (social security number
338	(SSN), individual taxpayer identification number (ITIN), adoption taxpayer
339	identification number (ATIN), or employer identification number (EIN)). However,
340	the issuer has reported your complete TIN to the IRS.
341	FATCA filing requirement. If the FATCA filing requirement box is checked, the
342	payer is reporting on this Form 1099 to satisfy its chapter 4 account reporting
343	requirement. You may also have a filing requirement. See the Instructions for
344	Form 8938.
345	Account number. May show an account or other unique number the payer
346	assigned to distinguish your account.
347	Payer’s Routing Transit Number (RTN). A payer may include the RTN to
348	identify the bank or financial institution where your account is held.
349	Box 1. Shows taxable interest paid to you during the calendar year by the payer.
350	This does not include interest shown in box 3. May also show the total amount
351	of the credits from clean renewable energy bonds, new clean renewable energy
352	bonds, qualified energy conservation bonds, qualified zone academy bonds,
353	qualified school construction bonds, and build America bonds that must be
354	included in your interest income. These amounts were treated as paid to you
355	during the calendar year on the credit allowance dates (March 15, June 15,
356	September 15, and December 15). For more information, see Form 8912. See
357	the instructions above for a taxable covered security acquired at a premium.
358	Box 2. Shows interest or principal forfeited because of early withdrawal of time
359	savings. You may deduct this amount to figure your adjusted gross income on
360	your income tax return. See the Instructions for Form 1040 to see where to take
361	the deduction.
362	
363	Box 3. Shows interest on U.S. Savings Bonds, Treasury bills, Treasury bonds,
364	and Treasury notes. This may or may not all be taxable. See Pub. 550. This
365	interest is exempt from state and local income taxes. This interest is not
366	included in box 1. See the instructions above for a taxable covered security
367	acquired at a premium.
368	Box 4. Shows backup withholding. Generally, a payer must backup withhold if
369	you did not furnish your TIN or you did not furnish the correct TIN to the payer.
370	See Form W-9. Include this amount on your income tax return as tax withheld.
371	Box 5. Any amount shown is your share of investment expenses of a singleclass REMIC. This amount is included in box 1. Note: This amount is not
372	deductible.
373	Box 6. Shows foreign tax paid. You may be able to claim this tax as a deduction
374	or a credit on your Form 1040 or 1040-SR. See your tax return instructions.
375	Box 7. Shows the country or U.S. territory to which the foreign tax was paid.
376	Box 8. Shows tax-exempt interest paid to you during the calendar year by the
377	payer. See how to report this amount in the Instructions for Form 1040. This
378	amount may be subject to backup withholding. See Box 4 above. See the
379	instructions above for a tax-exempt covered security acquired at a premium.
380	Box 9. Shows tax-exempt interest subject to the alternative minimum tax. This
381	amount is included in box 8. See the Instructions for Form 6251. See the
382	instructions above for a tax-exempt covered security acquired at a premium.
383	Box 10. For a taxable or tax-exempt covered security, if you made an election
384	under section 1278(b) to include market discount in income as it accrues and
385	you notified your payer of the election in writing in accordance with Regulations
386	section 1.6045-1(n)(5), shows the market discount that accrued on the debt
387	instrument during the year while held by you, unless it was reported on Form
388	1099-OID. For a taxable or tax-exempt covered security acquired on or after
389	January 1, 2015, accrued market discount will be calculated on a constant yield
390	basis unless you notified your payer in writing in accordance with Regulations
391	section 1.6045-1(n)(5) that you did not want to make a constant yield election for
392	market discount under section 1276(b). Report the accrued market discount on
393	your income tax return as directed in the Instructions for Form 1040. Market
394	discount on a tax-exempt security is includible in taxable income as interest
395	income.
