495	Instructions for Recipient (continued)
496	Box 11. For a taxable covered security (other than a U.S. Treasury
497	obligation), shows the amount of premium amortization allocable to
498	the interest payment(s), unless you notified the payer in writing in
499	accordance with Regulations section 1.6045-1(n)(5) that you did not
500	want to amortize bond premium under section 171. If an amount is
501	reported in this box, see the Instructions for Schedule B (Form 1040)
502	to determine the net amount of interest includible in income on Form
503	1040 or 1040-SR with respect to the security. If an amount is not
504	reported in this box for a taxable covered security acquired at a
505	premium and the payer is reporting premium amortization, the payer
506	has reported a net amount of interest in box 1. If the amount in box 11
507	is greater than the amount of interest paid on the covered security,
508	see Regulations section 1.171-2(a)(4).
509	Box 12. For a U.S. Treasury obligation that is a covered security,
510	shows the amount of premium amortization allocable to the interest
511	payment(s), unless you notified the payer in writing in accordance with
512	Regulations section 1.6045-1(n)(5) that you did not want to amortize
513	bond premium under section 171. If an amount is reported in this box,
514	see the Instructions for Schedule B (Form 1040) to determine the net
515	amount of interest includible in income on Form 1040 or 1040-SR with
516	respect to the U.S. Treasury obligation. If an amount is not reported in
517	this box for a U.S. Treasury obligation that is a covered security
518	acquired at a premium and the payer is reporting premium
519	amortization, the payer has reported a net amount of interest in box 3.
520	If the amount in box 12 is greater than the amount of interest paid on
521	the U.S. Treasury obligation, see Regulations section 1.171-2(a)(4).
522	
523	Box 13. For a tax-exempt covered security, shows the amount of
524	premium amortization allocable to the interest payment(s). If an
525	amount is reported in this box, see Pub. 550 to determine the net
526	amount of tax-exempt interest reportable on Form 1040 or 1040-SR.
527	If an amount is not reported in this box for a tax-exempt covered
528	security acquired at a premium, the payer has reported a net amount
529	of interest in box 8 or 9, whichever is applicable. If the amount in box
530	13 is greater than the amount of interest paid on the tax-exempt
531	covered security, the excess is a nondeductible loss. See Regulations
532	section 1.171-2(a)(4)(ii).
533	Box 14. Shows CUSIP number(s) for tax-exempt bond(s) on which
534	tax-exempt interest was paid, or tax credit bond(s) on which taxable
535	interest was paid or tax credit was allowed, to you during the calendar
536	year. If blank, no CUSIP number was issued for the bond(s).
537	Boxes 15–17. State tax withheld reporting boxes.
538	Nominees. If this form includes amounts belonging to another
539	person(s), you are considered a nominee recipient. Complete a
540	Form 1099-INT for each of the other owners showing the income
541	allocable to each. File Copy A of the form with the IRS. Furnish Copy
542	B to each owner. List yourself as the “payer” and the other owner(s)
543	as the “recipient.” File Form(s) 1099-INT with Form 1096 with the
544	Internal Revenue Service Center for your area. On Form 1096, list
545	yourself as the “filer.” A spouse is not required to file a nominee return
546	to show amounts owned by the other spouse.
547	Future developments. For the latest information about developments
548	related to Form 1099-INT and its instructions, such as legislation
549	enacted after they were published, go to www.irs.gov/Form1099INT.
550	Free File Program. Go to www.irs.gov/FreeFile to see if you qualify
551	for no-cost online federal tax preparation, e-filing, and direct deposit
552	or payment options.
